[38;2;124;124;124mwhich is faster than any polynomial.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, I need to make sure $f$ is continuous. The sum $\sum e^{n^2} \psi_n(x)$ — [0m[38;2;124;124;124msince the supports are disjoint (for large enough $n$, the intervals $[n - [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\delta_n, n+\delta_n]$ are disjoint), the sum is locally finite, and each term [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mis smooth, so $f$ is smooth (hence continuous).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, the supports $[n - \delta_n, n + \delta_n]$ for $n = 1, 2, 3, \ldots$ [0m[38;2;124;124;124mare disjoint as long as $\delta_n < 1/2$ for all $n$, which is certainly true [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msince $\delta_n = e^{-2n^2}$. So $f$ is smooth.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAnd $f(n) = e^{n^2} \cdot 1 = e^{n^2}$, which is not bounded by any polynomial.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the answer is NO, and this is the counterexample.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write this up cleanly.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me double-check the continuity argument more carefully. We need [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$T_f: \mathcal{S} \to \mathbb{C}$ to be continuous. A linear functional on $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathcal{S}$ is continuous iff there exist $C > 0$ and $N \in \mathbb{N}$ such [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthat $|T_f(\varphi)| \leq C \max_{|\alpha|,|\beta| \leq N} \rho_{\alpha,\beta}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(\varphi)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe showed $|T_f(\varphi)| \leq 2(\sum e^{-n^2}) \rho_{0,0}(\varphi)$. So taking [0m[38;2;124;124;124m$N = 0$ and $C = 2\sum e^{-n^2}$, this works. Great.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the answer is: **No**, it is not necessarily true. A continuous function that[0m[38;2;124;124;124mis a tempered distribution need not be polynomially bounded.[0m

